{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <queue>\n#include <unordered_set>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstdlib>\n#include <climits>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing ll = long long;\n\nstruct Step {\n    ll value;\n    int cost;\n    bool operator<(const Step& other) const {\n        return cost > other.cost;\n    }\n};\n\nunordered_set<ll> seen;\n\nbool is_seen(ll x) {\n    return seen.find(x) != seen.end();\n}\n\nStep u_upper(ll n) {\n    ll res = 0;\n    int cnt = 0;\n    while (res < n) {\n        res = res * 10 + 1;\n        ++cnt;\n    }\n    return {res, cnt};\n}\n\nStep u_upper(ll n, ll& res, int& cnt) {\n    res = 0;\n    cnt = 0;\n    while (res < n) {\n        res = res * 10 + 1;\n        ++cnt;\n    }\n    return {res, cnt};\n}\n\nStep upper_bound_step(ll n) {\n    ll res = 0;\n    int cnt = 0;\n    while (res * 10 + 1 <= n) {\n        res = res * 10 + 1;\n        ++cnt;\n    }\n    ll base = res;\n    int base_cnt = cnt;\n    while (res < n) {\n        res += base;\n        cnt += base_cnt;\n    }\n    return {res, cnt};\n}\n\nStep lower_bound_step(ll n) {\n    ll res = 0;\n    int cnt = 0;\n    while (res * 10 + 1 <= n) {\n        res = res * 10 + 1;\n        ++cnt;\n    }\n    ll base = res;\n    int base_cnt = cnt;\n    while (res + base <= n) {\n        res += base;\n        cnt += base_cnt;\n    }\n    return {res, cnt};\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios_base::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    ll n;\n    cin >> n;\n\n    priority_queue<Step> pq;\n    pq.push({n, 0});\n\n    while (!pq.empty()) {\n        Step cur = pq.top();\n        pq.pop();\n\n        if (cur.value == 0) {\n            cout << cur.cost << '\\n';\n            return 0;\n        }\n\n        if (is_seen(cur.value)) continue;\n        seen.insert(cur.value);\n\n        vector<Step> next_steps;\n        next_steps.push_back(lower_bound_step(cur.value));\n        next_steps.push_back(upper_bound_step(cur.value));\n        next_steps.push_back(u_upper(cur.value));\n\n        for (auto& ns : next_steps) {\n            ns.cost += cur.cost;\n            ns.value = llabs(cur.value - ns.value);\n            pq.push(ns);\n        }\n    }\n\n    cout << 0 << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static class Step {\n        long value;\n        int cost;\n\n        Step(long value, int cost) {\n            this.value = value;\n            this.cost = cost;\n        }\n    }\n\n    static class StepComparator implements Comparator<Step> {\n        public int compare(Step a, Step b) {\n            return Integer.compare(b.cost, a.cost);\n        }\n    }\n\n    static Set<Long> seen = new HashSet<>();\n\n    static boolean is_seen(long x) {\n        return seen.contains(x);\n    }\n\n    static Step u_upper(long n) {\n        long res = 0;\n        int cnt = 0;\n        while (res < n) {\n            res = res * 10 + 1;\n            ++cnt;\n        }\n        return new Step(res, cnt);\n    }\n\n    static Step upper_bound_step(long n) {\n        long res = 0;\n        int cnt = 0;\n        while (res * 10 + 1 <= n) {\n            res = res * 10 + 1;\n            ++cnt;\n        }\n        long base = res;\n        int base_cnt = cnt;\n        while (res < n) {\n            res += base;\n            cnt += base_cnt;\n        }\n        return new Step(res, cnt);\n    }\n\n    static Step lower_bound_step(long n) {\n        long res = 0;\n        int cnt = 0;\n        while (res * 10 + 1 <= n) {\n            res = res * 10 + 1;\n            ++cnt;\n        }\n        long base = res;\n        int base_cnt = cnt;\n        while (res + base <= n) {\n            res += base;\n            cnt += base_cnt;\n        }\n        return new Step(res, cnt);\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long n = scanner.nextLong();\n\n        PriorityQueue<Step> pq = new PriorityQueue<>(new StepComparator());\n        pq.offer(new Step(n, 0));\n\n        while (!pq.isEmpty()) {\n            Step cur = pq.poll();\n\n            if (cur.value == 0) {\n                System.out.println(cur.cost);\n                return;\n            }\n\n            if (is_seen(cur.value)) {\n                continue;\n            }\n            seen.add(cur.value);\n\n            List<Step> next_steps = new ArrayList<>();\n            next_steps.add(lower_bound_step(cur.value));\n            next_steps.add(upper_bound_step(cur.value));\n            next_steps.add(u_upper(cur.value));\n\n            for (Step ns : next_steps) {\n                ns.cost += cur.cost;\n                ns.value = Math.abs(cur.value - ns.value);\n                pq.offer(ns);\n            }\n        }\n\n        System.out.println(0);\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00011336160969221964, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -4.458328112377785e-05, -5.07818695